{"id":"mahabharata-12-007","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":7,"title":"सप्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 7 · Yudhishthira wishes to leave the world","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira grieves over the slaughter of kin and says he wants to live in the forest as an ascetic and give up the kingdom. He says that the victory was not worth the cost of so many dead.","kn":"ಬಂಧುಗಳ ಸಂಹಾರಕ್ಕಾಗಿ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ದುಃಖಿಸಿ ರಾಜ್ಯ ತೊರೆದು ವನದಲ್ಲಿ ತಪಸ್ವಿಯಾಗಿ ಬದುಕಲು ಬಯಸುವೆನೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಇಷ್ಟು ಜನ ಸತ್ತ ಬೆಲೆಗೆ ಜಯ ಯೋಗ್ಯವಲ್ಲವೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर स्वजनों के संहार पर शोक करते हैं और कहते हैं कि वे राज्य त्यागकर वन में तपस्वी बनकर रहना चाहते हैं। वे कहते हैं कि इतने मृतकों की क़ीमत पर यह विजय व्यर्थ है।","te":"బంధువుల సంహారానికి యుధిష్ఠిరుడు దుఃఖించి రాజ్యం వదిలి అడవిలో తపస్విగా జీవించాలని ఉందంటాడు. ఇంత మంది చనిపోయిన మూల్యానికి జయం విలువైనది కాదంటాడు.","ta":"உறவினரின் அழிவுக்கு யுதிஷ்டிரர் வருந்தி, நாட்டை விட்டுக் காட்டில் தவசியாக வாழ விரும்புவதாகக் கூறுகிறார். இத்தனை பேர் இறந்த விலைக்கு இவ்வெற்றி மதிப்பில்லை என்கிறார்.","ml":"ബന്ധുക്കളുടെ കൂട്ടക്കൊലയിൽ യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ വിലപിക്കുന്നു; രാജ്യം ഉപേക്ഷിച്ച് തപസ്വിയായി കാട്ടിൽ ജീവിക്കാൻ ആഗ്രഹിക്കുന്നുവെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു. ഇത്രയധികം മരണങ്ങളുടെ വിലയ്ക്ക് വിജയം വിലപ്പെട്ടതായിരുന്നില്ലെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.7; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"युधिष्ठिरस्तु धर्मात्मा शोकव्याकुलचेतनः ।\nशुशोच दुःखसंतप्तः स्मृत्वा कर्णं महारथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, of dharmic soul and mind shaken by grief, mourned, burning with sorrow, as he remembered Karna the great chariot-warrior."}},{"n":2,"text":"आविष्टो दुःखशोकाभ्यां निःश्वसंश्च पुनः पुनः ।\nदृष्ट्वार्जुनमुवाचेदं वचनं शोककर्शितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seized by sorrow and distress and sighing again and again, he looked at Arjuna and spoke these words, wasted with grief."}},{"n":3,"text":"यद्भैक्षमाचरिष्याम वृष्ण्यन्धकपुरे वयम् ।\nज्ञातीन्निष्पुरुषान्कृत्वा नेमां प्राप्स्याम दुर्गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said: Better that we had lived by begging alms in the city of the Vrishnis and Andhakas than to have emptied our kin of men and come to this evil state."}},{"n":4,"text":"अमित्रा नः समृद्धार्था वृत्तार्थाः कुरवः किल ।\nआत्मानमात्मना हत्वा किं धर्मफलमाप्नुमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is said that our enemies, the Kurus, had prospered and achieved their aims. Having killed ourselves by our own hands, what fruit of dharma do we gain?"}},{"n":5,"text":"धिगस्तु क्षात्रमाचारं धिगस्तु बलमौरसम् ।\nधिगस्त्वमर्षं येनेमामापदं गमिता वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shame on the warrior's way of life, shame on physical strength, shame on the intolerance by which we have fallen into this calamity!"}},{"n":6,"text":"साधु क्षमा दमः शौचमवैरोध्यममत्सरः ।\nअहिंसा सत्यवचनं नित्यानि वनचारिणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Forgiveness, self-control, purity, freedom from hostility and from envy, non-violence and truthful speech are always the practice of forest dwellers."}},{"n":7,"text":"वयं तु लोभान्मोहाच्च स्तम्भं मानं च संश्रिताः ।\nइमामवस्थामापन्ना राज्यलेशबुभुक्षया ॥","meaning":{"en":"But we, through greed and delusion, relied on rigidity and pride, and have come to this state from hunger for a scrap of kingdom."}},{"n":8,"text":"त्रैलोक्यस्यापि राज्येन नास्मान्कश्चित्प्रहर्षयेत् ।\nबान्धवान्निहतान्दृष्ट्वा पृथिव्यामामिषैषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not even rule over the three worlds could gladden us now, seeing our kinsmen slain, who on this earth were hunting for a morsel."}},{"n":9,"text":"ते वयं पृथिवीहेतोरवध्यान्पृथिवीसमान् ।\nसंपरित्यज्य जीवामो हीनार्था हतबान्धवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the sake of the earth we have abandoned those who were equal to the earth and not to be killed, and we live on, stripped of wealth and bereft of kin."}},{"n":10,"text":"आमिषे गृध्यमानानामशुनां नः शुनामिव ।\nआमिषं चैव नो नष्टमामिषस्य च भोजिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like dogs craving a scrap of meat, we have lost even the meat, and the eaters of the meat."}},{"n":11,"text":"न पृथिव्या सकलया न सुवर्णस्य राशिभिः ।\nन गवाश्वेन सर्वेण ते त्याज्या य इमे हताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not for the whole earth, nor heaps of gold, nor all the cattle and horses should we have given up these men who have been slain."}},{"n":12,"text":"संयुक्ताः काममन्युभ्यां क्रोधामर्षसमन्विताः ।\nमृत्युयानं समारुह्य गता वैवस्वतक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Joined by desire and anger, filled with rage and impatience, they boarded the vehicle of death and went to the abode of Vaivasvata (Yama)."}},{"n":13,"text":"बहु कल्याणमिच्छन्त ईहन्ते पितरः सुतान् ।\nतपसा ब्रह्मचर्येण वन्दनेन तितिक्षया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fathers strive for sons, wanting much good for them, through austerity, celibacy, reverence and patience."}},{"n":14,"text":"उपवासैस्तथेज्याभिर्व्रतकौतुकमङ्गलैः ।\nलभन्ते मातरो गर्भांस्तान्मासान्दश बिभ्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mothers obtain their unborn children with fasts, sacrifices, vows, rites of festivity and blessing, and carry them for ten months."}},{"n":15,"text":"यदि स्वस्ति प्रजायन्ते जाता जीवन्ति वा यदि ।\nसंभाविता जातबलास्ते दद्युर्यदि नः सुखम् ।\nइह चामुत्र चैवेति कृपणाः फलहेतुकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They hope that the children will be born safely and live, that being cherished and grown strong they might bring happiness both here and hereafter. Pitiable are those who act for the sake of a reward."}},{"n":16,"text":"तासामयं समारम्भो निवृत्तः केवलोऽफलः ।\nयदासां निहताः पुत्रा युवानो मृष्टकुण्डलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All that effort of theirs has ended fruitless, since their young sons with burnished earrings have been killed."}},{"n":17,"text":"अभुक्त्वा पार्थिवान्भोगानृणान्यनवदाय च ।\nपितृभ्यो देवताभ्यश्च गता वैवस्वतक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without enjoying the pleasures of kings, and without paying their debts to ancestors and gods, they have gone to the house of Vaivasvata."}},{"n":18,"text":"यदैषामङ्ग पितरौ जातौ काममयाविव ।\nसंजातबलरूपेषु तदैव निहता नृपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear brother, when the parents of these men were, as it were, made of desire, the princes were killed just when they had gained strength and beauty."}},{"n":19,"text":"संयुक्ताः काममन्युभ्यां क्रोधहर्षासमञ्जसाः ।\nन ते जन्मफलं किंचिद्भोक्तारो जातु कर्हिचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bound by desire and anger and confused by fury and joy, they never enjoyed any fruit of their birth, at any time."}},{"n":20,"text":"पाञ्चालानां कुरूणां च हता एव हि येऽहताः ।\nते वयं त्वधमाँल्लोकान्प्रपद्येम स्वकर्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of the Panchalas and the Kurus, those who were not killed are as good as dead. And we, by our own deeds, shall reach the lowest worlds."}},{"n":21,"text":"वयमेवास्य लोकस्य विनाशे कारणं स्मृताः ।\nधृतराष्ट्रस्य पुत्रेण निकृत्या प्रत्यपत्स्महि ॥","meaning":{"en":"We ourselves are remembered as the cause of this world's destruction. We were drawn into it by the trickery of Dhritarashtra's son."}},{"n":22,"text":"सदैव निकृतिप्रज्ञो द्वेष्टा मायोपजीवनः ।\nमिथ्यावृत्तः स सततमस्मास्वनपकारिषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was always scheming in deceit, hateful, living by illusion, and constantly false toward us, who had done him no wrong."}},{"n":23,"text":"अंशकामा वयं ते च न चास्माभिर्न तैर्जितम् ।\nन तैर्भुक्तेयमवनिर्न नार्यो गीतवादितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We wanted only our share, and so did they. Neither we nor they have truly won. They did not enjoy this earth, nor women, nor song and music."}},{"n":24,"text":"नामात्यसमितौ कथ्यं न च श्रुतवतां श्रुतम् ।\nन रत्नानि परार्ध्यानि न भूर्न द्रविणागमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They did not enjoy council with ministers, nor the learning of the learned, nor precious jewels, nor land, nor the arrival of wealth."}},{"n":25,"text":"ऋद्धिमस्मासु तां दृष्ट्वा विवर्णो हरिणः कृशः ।\nधृतराष्ट्रस्य नृपतेः सौबलेन निवेदितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing our prosperity, Duryodhana turned pale and thin like a deer, and Shakuni, Subala's son, reported it to King Dhritarashtra."}},{"n":26,"text":"तं पिता पुत्रगृद्धित्वादनुमेनेऽनये स्थितम् ।\nअनवेक्ष्यैव पितरं गाङ्गेयं विदुरं तथा ।\nअसंशयं धृतराष्ट्रो यथैवाहं तथा गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His father, out of attachment to his son, approved of him as he stood in wrongdoing, paying no heed to his father Bhishma or to Vidura. Beyond doubt, Dhritarashtra has fared as I have."}},{"n":27,"text":"अनियम्याशुचिं लुब्धं पुत्रं कामवशानुगम् ।\nपतितो यशसो दीप्ताद्घातयित्वा सहोदरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He did not restrain his impure, greedy son, who followed the pull of desire. Having had his own brothers killed, he fell from his blazing glory."}},{"n":28,"text":"इमौ वृद्धौ च शोकाग्नौ प्रक्षिप्य स सुयोधनः ।\nअस्मत्प्रद्वेषसंयुक्तः पापबुद्धिः सदैव हि ॥","meaning":{"en":"That Suyodhana, always of sinful mind and filled with hatred for us, has cast these two old parents into a fire of grief."}},{"n":29,"text":"को हि बन्धुः कुलीनः संस्तथा ब्रूयात्सुहृज्जने ।\nयथासावुक्तवान्क्षुद्रो युयुत्सुर्वृष्णिसंनिधौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"What well-born kinsman would speak to his friends the way that petty man, eager for battle, spoke in the presence of the Vrishnis?"}},{"n":30,"text":"आत्मनो हि वयं दोषाद्विनष्टाः शाश्वतीः समाः ।\nप्रदहन्तो दिशः सर्वास्तेजसा भास्करा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"By our own fault we have been ruined for endless years, scorching all quarters with our might, like suns."}},{"n":31,"text":"सोऽस्माकं वैरपुरुषो दुर्मन्त्रिप्रग्रहं गतः ।\nदुर्योधनकृते ह्येतत्कुलं नो विनिपातितम् ।\nअवध्यानां वधं कृत्वा लोके प्राप्ताः स्म वाच्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was our natural enemy, held in the grip of bad counsel. Because of Duryodhana our family has been brought down. Having killed those who should not be killed, we have earned blame in the world."}},{"n":32,"text":"कुलस्यास्यान्तकरणं दुर्मतिं पापकारिणम् ।\nराजा राष्ट्रेश्वरं कृत्वा धृतराष्ट्रोऽद्य शोचति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having made the sinful, evil-minded man, the destroyer of this family, ruler of the realm, King Dhritarashtra now grieves."}},{"n":33,"text":"हताः शूराः कृतं पापं विषयः स्वो विनाशितः ।\nहत्वा नो विगतो मन्युः शोको मां रुन्धयत्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The heroes are dead, the sin is done, our own country is destroyed. Though our rage is gone after killing them, this grief now chokes me."}},{"n":34,"text":"धनंजय कृतं पापं कल्याणेनोपहन्यते ।\nत्यागवांश्च पुनः पापं नालं कर्तुमिति श्रुतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhananjaya, sin that has been done is wiped out by good deeds, and, the scripture says, a man of renunciation can no longer commit sin."}},{"n":35,"text":"त्यागवाञ्जन्ममरणे नाप्नोतीति श्रुतिर्यदा ।\nप्राप्तवर्त्मा कृतमतिर्ब्रह्म संपद्यते तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the scripture says that the renouncer does not meet birth and death, then one who has found the path and made up his mind becomes Brahman."}},{"n":36,"text":"स धनंजय निर्द्वंद्वो मुनिर्ज्ञानसमन्वितः ।\nवनमामन्त्र्य वः सर्वान्गमिष्यामि परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"O Dhananjaya, free from the pairs of opposites, a sage endowed with knowledge, I will take leave of all of you, tormentor of foes, and go to the forest."}},{"n":37,"text":"न हि कृत्स्नतमो धर्मः शक्यः प्राप्तुमिति श्रुतिः ।\nपरिग्रहवता तन्मे प्रत्यक्षमरिसूदन ॥","meaning":{"en":"The scripture says that the whole of dharma cannot be attained by a man who clings to possessions. I have seen this plainly, slayer of enemies."}},{"n":38,"text":"मया निसृष्टं पापं हि परिग्रहमभीप्सता ।\nजन्मक्षयनिमित्तं च शक्यं प्राप्तुमिति श्रुतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I wished for possessions and so committed this sin. But it is said that the end of birth can be reached."}},{"n":39,"text":"स परिग्रहमुत्सृज्य कृत्स्नं राज्यं तथैव च ।\nगमिष्यामि विनिर्मुक्तो विशोको विज्वरस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore, casting off possessions and the whole kingdom, I shall go, released, free from grief and fever."}},{"n":40,"text":"प्रशाधि त्वमिमामुर्वीं क्षेमां निहतकण्टकाम् ।\nन ममार्थोऽस्ति राज्येन न भोगैर्वा कुरूत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rule this peaceful earth, with its thorns removed. For me there is no need of the kingdom or of enjoyments, best of the Kurus."}},{"n":41,"text":"एतावदुक्त्वा वचनं धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nव्युपारमत्ततः पार्थः कनीयान्प्रत्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this much, Yudhishthira, king of dharma, fell silent. Then the younger Partha, Arjuna, replied."}}]}]}